Growing logs, retained rows, caches, and objects need a counter-mechanism. Normal operation should not depend on repeated manual cleanup.

> The Steady State pattern says, for every mechanism that accumulates a resource, some other mechanism must recycle that resource.

Source: [Q08](/lore/durability-bibliography#q08); [B4](/lore/durability-bibliography#b4-release-it).

## Failure it prevents

Memory, storage, or latency fails after enough otherwise-successful operations.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Cache` and [Scope](/lore/scopes-own-resources) cover runtime lifetime. `PersistedQueue.layerCleanup` handles retained queue records. Durable domain data still needs a storage policy and maintenance owner.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Cache.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Scope.ts`, `packages/effect/src/persistence/PersistedQueue.ts`.

## How to check

Inspect growth over repeated work. Check retention against replay and dedupe requirements before deleting recovery evidence. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Queries need result bounds](/lore/queries-need-result-bounds), [Dead letters need a return path](/lore/dead-letters-need-a-return-path).

